### cr103-char-string-not-validated
# CR-103: none of the three items was implemented (conflicts, see NOTES.md). These
# vectors pin the documented behaviour that the requests asked to change.
# Item 1 / E7a [POL]: the character-string encoder does not validate UTF-8; the bytes
# are sent as given (overlong, surrogate, above U+10FFFF, truncated). Flip these to ERR
# only if the product owner changes E7a. (NaN refusal, item 2 / E5a, is already covered
# by real-nan-refused, double-nan-refused and double-nan-boundaries.)
enc_str c0af
enc_str eda080
enc_str f4908080
enc_str e282
---
OK 7300c0af
OK 7400eda080
OK 750500f4908080
OK 7300e282
### cr103-zero-integers
# Item 3 / E3, E12 [STD]: 0 has one content octet (ASHRAE 135 20.2.4 / 20.2.11);
# a zero-length Unsigned / Enumerated is rejected by the decoder (D4).
